# B4q — DOES A WALL'S DESCRIPTION REPRODUCE THE WALL?
#
# ⛔ **`hex_shape::wall_read_run` STATES IT AS A FACT ABOUT THE FIELD** — *"A-to-B and
# B-to-A mark the identical edges"* — and it is FALSE for this tree's stamper.
# `wall_stamp` takes its halfplane normal from the run's TANGENT, so reversing the walk
# flips which side a cell whose centre lies exactly ON the line falls on. A due-north
# wall in odd-r passes through alternate rows' centres, and exactly those flip.
#
# ⚠ **BOTH WALLS BELOW RECOVER TO THE SAME DESCRIPTION, `d6 p8`.** Only one of them is
# the field that description makes; the other reports `9 stray · 9 missing` of 11 marks.
# ⚠ **AND DUE EAST IS UNMOVED**, which is why the defect has survived: the corpus walks
# east.
#
#   make plan-view WORLD=b4q Q0=-4 Q1=5  R0=-3 R1=11 REF=2.0   # walked NORTH — clean
#   make plan-view WORLD=b4q Q0=5  Q1=14 R0=-3 R1=11 REF=2.0   # walked SOUTH — loud

echo --- a wall walked NORTH
at 0 0 0
verb run
at 0 9 0
verb run

echo --- and the same wall, nine hexes east, walked SOUTH
at 15 9 0
verb run
at 15 0 0
verb run
